{
 "id": "prog_chunk_growth",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "description": "P7-C of PROGRAM_SYNTHESIS_PLAN.md (PROGRAM_SYNTHESIS_P7C.md par.1.6): the SELF-TEACH tier of the idiom-grain chunk codebook. The agent grows its own write codebook from its own ACCEPTED programs: ckg_mark_scan DECIDES which Program nodes enter the chunk-learning flow (provenance program_synthesis, once per Program); the adapter (domains/prog_chunk_growth.scan_marked_programs) applies the marked decision MECHANICALLY -- the SAME fixed role/slot-abstraction walk the corpus miner uses -- ingesting Observation{kind:'prog_chunk', pk_status:'pending'} rows; ckg_recognize DECIDES a chunk is already held (standalone Covers over chunk_rels -- pattern-side WILD matches, so AntiUnify-merged mined entries recognize their variants; the pcon_recognize_covered precedent); ckg_mint DECIDES novelty (Not-Exists cover) and MINTS the write-codebook entry fully in-rule (bounded Term-computed name ckt_<snake(head)>_q<held-count>; attrs copied off the observation's own recorded facts; provenance self_taught) with the in-rule write_codebook_epoch bump (code_write_growth's own counter -- the established three-line epoch move; the curriculum re-arm rules already read this counter). ISOLATION: pk_status/kind prog_chunk attrs -- the frozen sd loop keys on 'status', the P3 loop on pc_status/kind prog_construction, so neither can see these observations; the minted entries' kind IS code_write_construction because that is the ONLY kind ps_propose reads (proposability is the point). ONE-MINT-PER-PASS: the pcon_mint Argmin-survivor serializer (measured engine fact: the non-batch attempt path is SNAPSHOT-DRAIN -- two novel observations in one pass would both mint before either saw the other's entry; the Argmin guard makes exactly one apply per pass, every other candidate re-decides against the grown codebook next pass). NO edit to seeds/program_synthesis.json: ckg_mark_scan only READS the Program nodes that seed's ps_accept produces.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "prog_chunk_growth",
  "description": "an accepted program's recurring sub-trees are chunk observations; a novel chunk (nothing held covers it) becomes a new proposable write-codebook entry, self-taught; the run_rules fixpoint is the recognize-or-grow loop at idiom grain."
 },
 "nodes": [],
 "edges": [],
 "productions": [],
 "rules": [
  {
   "name": "ckg_mark_scan",
   "comment": "An accepted Program{provenance:'program_synthesis'} enters the chunk-learning flow ONCE (ck_scan_marked guard). The DECISION (which programs feed self-teach) is this rule's; the extraction walk is the adapter's mechanical application (the P3 decision-in-rules / application-in-adapter split).",
   "batch": true,
   "match": [
    [
     "g",
     "accepted_program",
     "p"
    ]
   ],
   "where": {
    "type": "And",
    "items": [
     {
      "type": "Eq",
      "a": {
       "type": "Attr",
       "node": {
        "type": "Var",
        "name": "p"
       },
       "key": "provenance"
      },
      "b": {
       "type": "Lit",
       "value": "program_synthesis"
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Not",
      "arg": {
       "type": "Eq",
       "a": {
        "type": "Attr",
        "node": {
         "type": "Var",
         "name": "p"
        },
        "key": "ck_scan_marked"
       },
       "b": {
        "type": "Lit",
        "value": 1.0
       }
      }
     }
    ]
   },
   "effects": [
    [
     "set_attr",
     "p",
     "ck_scan_marked",
     1.0
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
